  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalDisjoint">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">interval disjoint</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="es">intervalo disjunto</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">If a proper interval T1 is intervalDisjoint another proper interval T2, then the beginning of T1 is after the end of T2, or the end of T1 is before the beginning of T2, i.e. the intervals do not overlap in any way, but their ordering relationship is not known.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="es">Si un intervalo propio T1 es disjunto con otro intervalo propio T2, entonces el principio de T1 está después del final de T2, o el final de T1 está antes que el principio de T2, es decir, los intervalos no se solapan de ninguna forma, aunque su relación de orden no se conozca.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#ProperInterval"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#ProperInterval"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">If a proper interval T1 is intervalDisjoint another proper interval T2, then the beginning of T1 is after the end of T2, or the end of T1 is before the beginning of T2, i.e. the intervals do not overlap in any way, but their ordering relationship is not known.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="es">Si un intervalo propio T1 es disjunto con otro intervalo propio T2, entonces el principio de T1 está después del final de T2, o el final de T1 está antes que el principio de T2, es decir, los intervalos no se solapan de ninguna forma, aunque su relación de orden no se conozca.</skos:definition>
    <skos:note xml:lang="en">This interval relation is not included in the 13 basic relationships defined in Allen (1984), but is defined in (T.3) as the union of :intervalBefore v :intervalAfter . However, that is outside OWL2 expressivity, so is implemented as an explicit property, with :intervalBefore , :intervalAfter as sub-properties</skos:note>
    <skos:note xml:lang="es">Esta relación entre intervalos no estaba incluida en las 13 relaciones básicas definidas por Allen (1984), pero está definida en T.3 como la unión de 'intervalo anterior' con 'intervalo posterior'. Sin embargo, esto está fuera de la expresividad de OWL2, por tanto, está implementado como una propiedad explícita, con 'intervalo anterior' e 'intervalo posterior' como sub-propiedades.</skos:note>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/choiceAfterStep">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">choice after step</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The planned source step after which the choice is considered. Alternative transitionFrom values should identify this step.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/ExclusiveChoice"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="https://www.michaeldebellis.com/supply_chain_model/CollaborationStep"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://www.in2use.com/method_omega/Method_Omega">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.org/net/p-plan#Plan"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Method Omega</rdfs:label>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Method Omega</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Reusable Method Omega development methodology, transcribed from Michael DeBellis's supplied diagram. This excerpt expands Requirements Acquisition only. No project-specific plan, execution, participant assignment, scheduled date, or duration estimate is asserted.</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Horizontal solid arrows are finish-to-start requirements. The No branch is a possible rework transition, not an unconditional reverse precedence assertion. Precedence applies to the matching pass through the plan, not every pair of Activities sharing the source and target Step definitions. Unspecified dependencies do not assert concurrency.</skos:scopeNote>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalEquals">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">interval equals</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="es">intervalo igual</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">If a proper interval T1 is intervalEquals another proper interval T2, then the beginning of T1 is coincident with the beginning of T2, and the end of T1 is coincident with the end of T2.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="es">Si un intervalo propio T1 es igual a otro intervalo propio T2, entonces el principio de T1 coincide con el principio de T2, y el final de T1 coincide con el final de T2.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#ProperInterval"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#ProperInterval"/>
    <owl:propertyDisjointWith rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#intervalIn"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">If a proper interval T1 is intervalEquals another proper interval T2, then the beginning of T1 is coincident with the beginning of T2, and the end of T1 is coincident with the end of T2.</skos:definition>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="es">Si un intervalo propio T1 es igual a otro intervalo propio T2, entonces el principio de T1 coincide con el principio de T2, y el final de T1 coincide con el final de T2.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#Year">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
